.git
.github
.claude
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.venv
venv
env

# Local store / generated artifacts -- never belong in a server image
memory/
benchmark/
tests/
assets/

# The client package stays out of the server image -- with named exceptions,
# one per module hub/ actually imports. Both exist for the same reason: the
# Hub and the client must produce the SAME numbers, and a near-copy that
# drifted would not fail loudly, it would return confident and wrong ones.
#
#   overlap.py     hub/commons.py -- MinHash. Signatures are only comparable
#                  if both sides draw the same permutations.
#   experiment.py  hub/outcomes.py -- the outcome statistics. A drifted copy
#                  would make the customer's own `commontrace experiment` and
#                  the operator's `hub.manage outcomes` disagree about the
#                  same fleet, which finishes the number as evidence.
#   retrieval.py   hub/bench_retrieval.py -- the LOCAL retrieval tier, used
#   _lexical.py    as the reference the Hub's own recall is reported against.
#                  Same reason again, in its sharpest form: that comparison
#                  is the entire finding (0.0% vs 84.8% recall@1 on identical
#                  records), and a reimplemented reference would be measuring
#                  the Hub against something no customer runs.
#                  _lexical.py is retrieval.py's own import, not a separate
#                  decision.
#
# All four are pure stdlib, so they add source to the image and no dependency.
#
# KEEP THIS LIST IN SYNC WITH THE IMPORTS. A module missing here does not
# break the build -- it breaks container START, with an ImportError on code
# that imports fine in every test run and every editable install. That is
# invisible until a deployment tries to boot, so
# hub/tests/test_image_contents.py asserts the two lists match and runs in
# every CI job, not only the Docker ones.
#
# Excluding the contents rather than the directory itself, so the negations
# below can re-include specific files (an excluded *directory* is never
# traversed, so `!commontrace/x.py` under a bare `commontrace/` rule would
# not match).
commontrace/**
!commontrace/__init__.py
!commontrace/overlap.py
!commontrace/experiment.py
# The validity audit that runs in front of every causal number
# (hub/crud.py:causal_effects). Without it the Hub answers
# fleet_outcomes with effect sizes and no way to tell whether the
# sample can support them -- and the container would not even start,
# because crud.py imports it at module level.
!commontrace/integrity.py
!commontrace/retrieval.py
!commontrace/_lexical.py

# Secrets must come from the platform's secret store, never be baked in
.env
hub/.env
*.env
!hub/.env.example
